                <h2>适用场景</h2>
<p>当你的团队出现以下情况时，需要启动账户分层管理：</p>
<ul>
<li>同时运营 5 个以上广告账户</li>
<li>团队成员人均负责 3+ 账户</li>
<li>账户表现差异明显但管理方式相同</li>
<li>投放预算从数千到数万不等</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>第一步：建立分层评估维度</h2>
<blockquote>
<p>不以预算大小论英雄，而以投入产出比和战略价值综合评判。</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>评估维度清单</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>维度</th>
<th>权重</th>
<th>说明</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>近 30 天 ROAS</td>
<td>30%</td>
<td>核心盈利指标</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>账户稳定性</td>
<td>20%</td>
<td>波动幅度、违规记录</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>预算规模</td>
<td>20%</td>
<td>可提升空间</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>增长潜力</td>
<td>15%</td>
<td>市场容量、品类趋势</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>战略重要性</td>
<td>15%</td>
<td>品牌建设、竞争占位</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>操作步骤</h3>
<ol>
<li>导出所有账户近 30 天数据（花费、转化数、转化成本、ROAS）</li>
<li>收集账户历史违规次数和封号风险</li>
<li>对照行业基准设定各维度评分标准</li>
<li>加权计算各账户综合得分</li>
<li>按得分排序，确定分层结果</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>第二步：划分账户等级并匹配资源</h2>
<p>根据综合得分，将账户划分为三个等级：</p>
<h3>A 级账户（占比 20%，消耗 50% 精力）</h3>
<p><strong>特征：</strong> 综合得分前 20%，ROAS 稳定高于均值 30%</p>
<p><strong>资源匹配：</strong><br />
- 专人专管，每日至少一次深度分析<br />
- 优先测试新素材、新定向<br />
- 分配资深优化师</p>
<h3>B 级账户（占比 50%，消耗 35% 精力）</h3>
<p><strong>特征：</strong> 综合得分居中，有明确优化空间</p>
<p><strong>资源匹配：</strong><br />
- 标准化 SOP 执行，重点关注下降指标<br />
- 周度复盘，批量调整<br />
- 分配中级运营</p>
<h3>C 级账户（占比 30%，消耗 15% 精力）</h3>
<p><strong>特征：</strong> 综合得分靠后，亏损或增长乏力</p>
<p><strong>资源匹配：</strong><br />
- 最小成本维持，观察 2 周<br />
- 无明显改善则暂停或关闭<br />
- 新人练手或自动化托管</p>
<hr />
<h2>第三步：建立动态调整机制</h2>
<p>分层不是一次性工作，需要月度复盘与动态调整：</p>
<h3>调整触发条件</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>升级条件：</strong> 连续 4 周 ROAS 提升超过 20%，可申请升级</li>
<li><strong>降级条件：</strong> 连续 2 周 ROAS 下降超过 15%，触发降级审查</li>
<li><strong>紧急降级：</strong> 出现账户被封、严重违规，立即降至 C 级</li>
</ul>
<h3>月度复盘流程</h3>
<ol>
<li>每月 5 日前导出上月账户数据</li>
<li>按评估维度重新计算综合得分</li>
<li>与上期对比，确认调整名单</li>
<li>内部通知资源重新分配计划</li>
<li>更新管理看板和分工表</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>常见问题</h2>
<p><strong>Q：账户数量少是否需要分层？</strong><br />
少于 5 个账户时，建议先按产品线或地区简单分组，分层意义不大。</p>
<p><strong>Q：如何处理新接手账户？</strong><br />
新账户默认进入 C 级观察期，给予 4 周测试窗口后再正式分层。</p>
<p><strong>Q：跨平台账户如何统一分层？</strong><br />
建议先按平台分别分层，同平台内执行统一标准，避免跨平台对比失真。</p>
<hr />
<h2>执行清单</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] 整理所有账户近 30 天数据</li>
<li>[ ] 按评估维度打分</li>
<li>[ ] 划分 A/B/C 等级</li>
<li>[ ] 更新分工表和资源分配</li>
<li>[ ] 设置月度复盘提醒</li>
</ul>
            </div>
            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>When to Apply This SOP</h2>
<p>Implement account tiering when your team faces:</p>
<ul>
<li>Managing 5+ advertising accounts simultaneously</li>
<li>Each team member handling 3+ accounts</li>
<li>Significant performance differences but identical management approaches</li>
<li>Budgets ranging from thousands to tens of thousands</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Establish Evaluation Dimensions</h2>
<blockquote>
<p>Don't judge accounts solely by budget size; evaluate based on ROI and strategic value.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>Evaluation Dimension Checklist</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Dimension</th>
<th>Weight</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Last 30-day ROAS</td>
<td>30%</td>
<td>Core profitability metric</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Account Stability</td>
<td>20%</td>
<td>Volatility, violation records</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Budget Scale</td>
<td>20%</td>
<td>Growth potential</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Growth Potential</td>
<td>15%</td>
<td>Market capacity, category trends</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Strategic Importance</td>
<td>15%</td>
<td>Brand building, competitive positioning</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
<ol>
<li>Export all accounts' last 30-day data (spend, conversions, CPA, ROAS)</li>
<li>Gather account historical violation counts and ban risks</li>
<li>Set scoring standards for each dimension against industry benchmarks</li>
<li>Calculate weighted composite scores for all accounts</li>
<li>Rank by score to determine tier assignments</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Assign Account Tiers and Match Resources</h2>
<p>Based on composite scores, divide accounts into three tiers:</p>
<h3>Tier A Accounts (20% of total, 50% of effort)</h3>
<p><strong>Characteristics:</strong> Top 20% composite score, ROAS consistently 30%+ above average</p>
<p><strong>Resource Allocation:</strong><br />
- Dedicated manager, daily in-depth analysis<br />
- Priority for testing new creatives and targeting<br />
- Assign senior specialists</p>
<h3>Tier B Accounts (50% of total, 35% of effort)</h3>
<p><strong>Characteristics:</strong> Middle-tier scores, clear optimization opportunities</p>
<p><strong>Resource Allocation:</strong><br />
- Standardized SOP execution, focus on declining metrics<br />
- Weekly reviews, batch adjustments<br />
- Assign mid-level operators</p>
<h3>Tier C Accounts (30% of total, 15% of effort)</h3>
<p><strong>Characteristics:</strong> Bottom-tier scores, loss-making or stalled growth</p>
<p><strong>Resource Allocation:</strong><br />
- Minimal cost maintenance, 2-week observation<br />
- No improvement = pause or close<br />
- Training for new hires or automated托管</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Establish Dynamic Adjustment Mechanism</h2>
<p>Tier assignments aren't one-time decisions—they require monthly reviews and adjustments:</p>
<h3>Adjustment Triggers</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Upgrade:</strong> ROAS improved for 4 consecutive weeks by 20%+</li>
<li><strong>Downgrade:</strong> ROAS declined for 2 consecutive weeks by 15%+</li>
<li><strong>Emergency Downgrade:</strong> Account ban or serious violations = immediate Tier C</li>
</ul>
<h3>Monthly Review Process</h3>
<ol>
<li>Export previous month's data by the 5th</li>
<li>Recalculate composite scores by evaluation dimensions</li>
<li>Compare with previous period, confirm adjustment list</li>
<li>Internal notification of resource reallocation plan</li>
<li>Update management dashboard and task assignments</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: Is tiering necessary with fewer accounts?</strong><br />
With fewer than 5 accounts, simple grouping by product line or region is recommended. Full tiering has limited value.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How to handle newly接手 accounts?</strong><br />
New accounts enter Tier C observation period by default, formally tiered after a 4-week test window.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How to unify tiering across platforms?</strong><br />
Recommended to tier separately by platform first, applying uniform standards within each platform to avoid cross-platform comparison distortion.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Execution Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Compile all accounts' last 30-day data</li>
<li>[ ] Score by evaluation dimensions</li>
<li>[ ] Assign A/B/C tiers</li>
<li>[ ] Update task assignments and resource allocation</li>
<li>[ ] Set monthly review reminders</li>
</ul>
